WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:06.550
Uncomfortable reshoots. Accusations of dishonesty.
Disagreements about directors. These are just

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:11.559
some of the reasons these actors were miserable
while shooting a "Thor" movie. Keep watching

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:15.299
to learn everything you need to know about
the "who" and "why."

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:19.550
The most recent "Thor" movies are known for
being lighter and more fun than many other

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.320
MCU films. The latest entry, "Thor: Love and
Thunder," is no exception, from its Guardians

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:29.080
of the Galaxy hijinks to the hilarious giant
screaming goats.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.210
"And giant goats!"

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.330
"Look at those! They are wonderful!"

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:39.630
Reviewers have praised this lighthearted take.
Collider's Perri Nemiroff posted about the

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.630
film,

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:45.391
"LOADS of laughs (my face legit hurts), menace
of Christian Bale's Gorr is chilling, but

00:00:45.391 --> 00:00:49.720
most of all loved that it's a film brimming
with good vibes &amp; heart."

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:53.870
But that doesn't mean the "Thor" movies have
always been fun to make for all the actors

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.410
involved. While these films look like they
must have been a blast to create, the intense

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.890
level of pressure involved — along with
issues behind the scenes — means that it

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.210
wasn't all fun for everyone on set.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:09.630
Take, for example, Christopher Eccleston.
You may know him best for playing the Ninth

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.790
Doctor with the catchphrase,

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.210
"Fantastic!"

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:17.579
He famously did not think his experience on
"Doctor Who" was fantastic, though. He also

00:01:17.579 --> 00:01:21.700
didn't like being Malekith the Accursed, the
ruler of the Dark Elves in "Thor: The Dark

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:22.700
World."

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:27.420
For his Thor woes, the actor blames a bit
of dishonesty during negotiations. He told

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.469
Metro that he was led to believe there would
only be a little makeup. He said,

00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:36.409
"What they didn't say was that it'd be seven
hours of it, which was very dishonest of them.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:39.670
That was a miserable experience and a dreadful
performance."

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:44.530
Metro isn't the only media outlet he complained
to. He explained to "The Guardian" how horrible

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:49.880
his experiences were on both "G. I. Joe: The
Rise of Cobra," in which he played Destro,

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.869
and "Thor: The Dark World," saying both roles
were regrettable.

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:57.410
However, Eccleston has also made clear that
he has no beef with the cast and crew of "The

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:02.290
Dark World," singling out director Alan Taylor
and star Chris Hemsworth for praise. He told

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:03.290
Metro,

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:07.450
"I loved working with Alan — he's a great
director. And Hemsworth was fantastic. A generous

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.550
actor who really had his feet on the ground."

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:14.200
Considering he's appeared in multiple MCU
films, you might think Idris Elba, who plays

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.450
the Asgardian Heimdall, the former guardian
of the Bifrost Bridge, had a great time. Yet,

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.940
like Eccleston, he said some harsh things
about "Thor: The Dark World," specifically.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:28.620
Elba told The Telegraph in 2014 that right
after he finished playing activist Nelson

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.730
Mandela in "Mandela: Long Walk to Freedom,"
he was contractually obligated to return to

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:38.750
the 2013 "Thor" sequel for reshoots. This
included an uncomfortable scene in which he

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.470
was falling from a spaceship. Elba explained,

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:45.480
"I was like, 'This is torture, man. I don't
want to do this. Twenty-four hours ago, I

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.820
was Mandela. [...] Then there I was, in this
stupid harness, with this wig and this sword

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.950
and these contact lenses. It ripped my heart
out."

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:57.350
Even so, Elba has also praised Taylor and
his vision for "The Dark World" in a Flicks

00:02:57.350 --> 00:03:02.460
and the City interview. And given his continued
presence in the MCU after that, it seems like

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:06.730
his issues with the "Thor" reshoots might've
been more situational rather than a deeper

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:07.730
resentment.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:12.900
In fact, it's clear the actor wants more work
in the Marvel universe, not less. In 2017,

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.430
he told Entertainment Weekly,

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:18.750
"I like what I have, but I also wish that
I had a bigger character in the Marvel universe."

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.540
"There is always hope."

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.600
One more actor who wasn't thrilled with "The
Dark World" was Natalie Portman, who became

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.210
disenchanted with the "Thor" franchise and
reportedly declined to show up for reshoots

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:36.700
for the sequel. She didn't appear in any more
Marvel films — setting aside a cameo that

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:40.730
reused "Dark World" footage in "Avengers:
Endgame" — until "Love and Thunder."

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:46.470
She also made her beef public. In 2011, the
Hollywood Reporter reported that Portman was

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:50.790
"deeply unhappy" that her choice for the sequel's
director, Patty Jenkins, who would go on to

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:55.310
direct "Wonder Woman," was ousted by Marvel
following creative differences.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:59.370
The publication said that Portman had already
been on the fence about returning to the franchise

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:03.370
because she wanted to spend time with her
family, while Vulture noted that she gained

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:08.820
a renewed excitement about the role when Jenkins
was hired. Once Jenkins was gone, this presumably

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:13.700
changed. Us reports that when she said filming
conflicts prevented her from returning for

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:18.749
reshoots, Hemsworth's real-life wife Elsa
Pataky filled in for her. In an interview

00:04:18.749 --> 00:04:21.759
with the Wall Street Journal in 2016, Portman
said,

00:04:21.759 --> 00:04:26.490
"I don't know if one day they'll ask for an
'Avengers 7' or whatever, I have no idea,

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:30.430
but as far as I know, I'm done. It was a great
thing to be a part of."

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:34.250
But she obviously had enough fond memories
to finally come back to the role in "Love

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:39.050
and Thunder," once Jane was finally given
a bigger role. According to CNN, it reportedly

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:43.530
only took one meeting for Taika Waititi to
convince her to sign up again.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.669
"Quite a reunion, huh?"

